1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:07,685
The brush clears a palm leaf. It is covered with Tamil verses, scratched with an iron stylus.

2
00:00:07,685 --> 00:00:14,058
These poems, collected much later, describe kings, wars, love and trade in the far south.

3
00:00:14,058 --> 00:00:17,074
What did a poet remember about the south?

4
00:00:34,483 --> 00:00:42,812
How do we know? Sangam literature is the main source. Archaeologists dug up the port of Arikamedu and the town of Keezhadi.

5
00:00:42,812 --> 00:00:46,558
And Roman coins found in the south show the trade.

6
00:01:02,483 --> 00:01:05,176
Tamilakam was the land of the Tamils.

7
00:01:05,176 --> 00:01:14,272
Three kingdoms ruled it: the Cholas of Uraiyur, with the tiger, the Pandyas of Madurai, with the fish, and the Cheras of Vanji, with the bow.

8
00:01:14,272 --> 00:01:22,874
The Sangam literature gives us this world. The Tolkappiyam is a grammar. The Ettuthokai and Pattuppattu are collections of poems.

9
00:01:22,874 --> 00:01:27,471
The epics Silappadikaram and Manimekalai were composed a little later.

10
00:01:27,471 --> 00:01:32,373
Tradition says that poets met in assemblies, or Sangams, at Madurai.

11
00:01:32,373 --> 00:01:36,652
Modern scholars treat that as tradition, not as settled history.

12
00:01:36,652 --> 00:01:44,516
The poems divide the land into five landscapes, or tinais: hills, forest, farmland, seashore and desert.

13
00:01:44,516 --> 00:01:47,142
Each has its own moods and gods.

14
00:01:47,142 --> 00:01:54,779
Famous kings include Karikala Chola, who is credited with building embankments on the Kaveri, and Senguttuvan Chera.

15
00:01:54,779 --> 00:02:03,177
Trade was rich. Pepper, pearls and cloth went west. Roman gold coins came back in return.

16
00:02:19,117 --> 00:02:28,936
Old name, new name. The Sangam age is set in Tamilakam, the land of the Tamils. It covers most of present Tamil Nadu and Kerala.

17
00:02:28,936 --> 00:02:32,867
The old name is the name the poems themselves use.

18
00:02:48,783 --> 00:02:57,149
Carve this tip into memory. Chola tiger, Pandya fish. Chera bow. Three kingdoms, three emblems.

19
00:02:57,149 --> 00:03:01,729
Add Uraiyur, Madurai and Vanji, and you have the south.

20
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:33,268
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Name the oldest Tamil grammar. The answer: the Tolkappiyam. Number two.

21
00:03:33,268 --> 00:03:49,619
What is the emblem of the Pandyas? The answer: the fish. Number three. Which foreign coins are found in southern hoards?

22
00:03:49,619 --> 00:03:59,863
The answer: Roman coins. Now one line for Mains. Discuss the Sangam age as a source of ancient Tamil society.

23
00:04:19,783 --> 00:04:27,899
The palm leaf goes into its case. Poets once scratched their verses on leaves like this. Three facts to take away.

24
00:04:27,899 --> 00:04:37,902
Tamil verses on a palm leaf. Sangam poems, about 300 BCE to 300 CE. Chola, Chera and Pandya kingdoms.

25
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:41,906
Next gallery: Gandhara and Mathura.

